=comment Package: Gtk4, C-Source: csssection
use v6.d;

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#--[Class Description]----------------------------------------------------------
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

=begin rakudoc
=TITLE Gnome::Gtk4::N-CssSection
=head1 Description

Defines a part of a CSS document.

Because sections are nested into one another, you can use
[method C<$CssSection>.get_parent] to get the containing region.

=begin comment

=begin code

=head3 Example

Example use of module Gnome::Gtk4::CssSection

=begin code
=end code

=end code

=end comment

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#--[Class Initialization]-------------------------------------------------------
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

=begin rakudoc
=head1 Class initialization

=head2 new

=head3 :native-object

Create an object using a native object from an object of the same type found elsewhere. See also B<Gnome::N::TopLevelSupportClass>.

  multi method new ( N-Object() :$native-object! )

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 new-csssection

Creates a new B<Gnome::Gtk4::N-CssSection> referring to the section
in the given B<file> from the B<start> location to the
B<end> location.

=begin code
method new-csssection ( N-Object() $file, N-Object $start, N-Object $end --> Gnome::Gtk4::CssSection )
=end code

=item $file; The file this section refers to.
=item $start; The start location
=item $end; The end location

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 new-with-bytes

Creates a new B<Gnome::Gtk4::N-CssSection> referring to the section
in the given B<file> or the given B<bytes> from the B<start> location to the
B<end> location.

=begin code
method new-with-bytes ( N-Object() $file, N-Object $bytes, N-Object $start, N-Object $end --> Gnome::Gtk4::CssSection )
=end code

=item $file; The file this section refers to.
=item $bytes; The bytes this sections refers to
=item $start; The start location
=item $end; The end location

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#--[Methods]--------------------------------------------------------------------
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

=begin rakudoc
=head1 Methods
=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 get-bytes

Gets the bytes that C<$section> was parsed from.

=begin code
method get-bytes (--> N-Object )
=end code

Return value; the B<Gnome::Glib::N-Bytes> from which the B<section>
  was parsed. 

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 get-end-location

Returns the location in the CSS document where this section ends.

=begin code
method get-end-location (--> N-Object )
=end code

Return value; The end location of
  this section. 

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 get-file

Gets the file that C<$section> was parsed from.

If no such file exists, for example because the CSS was loaded via
L<.load-from-data() in class Gnome|/content-docs/api2/reference/Gtk4/Gnome#load-from-data>, then undefined is returned.

=begin code
method get-file (--> N-Object )
=end code

Return value; the L<Gnome::Gio::File|/content-docs/api2/reference/Gio/File> from which the B<section>
  was parsed. 

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 get-parent

Gets the parent section for the given B<section>.

The parent section is the section that contains this B<section>. A special
case are sections of  type B<GTK_CSS_SECTION_DOCUMENT>. Their parent will
either be undefined if they are the original CSS document that was loaded by
L<.load-from-file() in class Gnome|/content-docs/api2/reference/Gtk4/Gnome#load-from-file> or a section of type
B<GTK_CSS_SECTION_IMPORT> if it was loaded with an ` C<$import>` rule from
a different file.

=begin code
method get-parent (--> N-Object )
=end code

Return value; the parent section. 

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 get-start-location

Returns the location in the CSS document where this section starts.

=begin code
method get-start-location (--> N-Object )
=end code

Return value; The start location of
  this section. 

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 print

Prints the B<section> into B<string> in a human-readable form.

This is a form like B<gtk>.css:32:1-23` to denote line 32, characters
1 to 23 in the file B<gtk>.css`.

=begin code
method print ( N-Object $string )
=end code

=item $string; a B<Gnome::Glib::N-String> to print to

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 ref

Increments the reference count on B<section>.

=begin code
method ref (--> N-Object )
=end code

Return value; the CSS section itself.. 

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 to-string

Prints the section into a human-readable text form using
L<.print()|#print>.

=begin code
method to-string (--> Str )
=end code

Return value; A new string.. 

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 unref

Decrements the reference count on B<section>, freeing the
structure if the reference count reaches 0.

=begin code
method unref ( )
=end code

=end rakudoc

